      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HARTSHORN (3) brings the right blend of current form and race fitness. His fourth in a BM70 at this track last week reads better than the bare margin after he began slowly and met interference, and he had won strongly on soft ground at this venue the start before. ROWEINER'S DANCE (1) resumes with an easy Townsville trial win behind him and outstanding track-and-distance figures. Rates the main threat. NOTTINGTON PRINCE (8) is also a danger, with a win and two placings from three runs this season and a strong record at this track and distance. ADMITTED (4) has a forgive run from Ewan after racing wide throughout, while his Mackay third in CL6 grade keeps him in the mix if he produces that level again. RUSSIAN MINT (2) is another track and trip specialist resuming and warrants obvious consideration.",
